# templates/.vercelignore.template — Vercel Ignore Template
# Copy to ./.vercelignore and adjust. Lines here are excluded from Vercel builds.
# Raw: https://vercel.com/docs/projects/project-configuration#vercelignore
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ⚠️  WARNING: .wiki/ bundle rule — read before enabling .wiki/
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# If any api/*.ts does fs.readFileSync on wiki files (e.g., get_leak_constants → .wiki/wiki/topics/knowledge-base.md),
# you MUST NOT exclude .wiki/ without bundling via vercel.json:
#
#   vercel.json → "functions": { "api/mcp.ts": { "includeFiles": ".wiki/wiki/topics/**" } }
#
# If you keep ".wiki/" below, production will ENOENT:
#   Error: wiki SSOT 읽기 실패 (.wiki/wiki/topics/knowledge-base.md): ENOENT
# Fix: either (A) remove ".wiki/" from ignore and keep it deployed, or (B) keep ignore but add includeFiles.
# Dev note: `vercel dev` respects vercel.json bundling, `vite dev` does NOT run api/*.ts — wiki ENOENT is prod-only if misconfigured.
# See templates/vercel.json.template for example.

# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.vite-react-ssg-temp/

# Environment and provider-local state
.env
.env.*
*.local
.vercel

# Harness vault — keep or bundle? see ⚠️ above
# If api/*.ts reads wiki, comment the next line OR add vercel.json includeFiles.
.wiki/

